  "body": "Sew XYUV rulings consistently across planes when one plane heals a swallowtail and the other plane does not.\n\n## Context\n\nWhen XY trims a tight corner fillet or bridges a shallow slot, its offset ring `wu`/`wl` loses arc length while UV keeps the full arc. Pairing directly by trimmed offset arc length (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/pairing.rs`) shifts rulings out of phase around the contour and can trigger `folds`, `crossing`, or `too_far`. Also, `ruled_widen::away` (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ruled_widen.rs`) computes widening directions from unhealed `given` edges, which can reverse steps near a trimmed vertex.\n\n## What this does\n\n- Build a monotone preimage map from each healed offset ring's edge midpoints and vertices back to arc positions on its original input profile `given`.\n- Collapse any excised input span `(s_a, s_b)` to the corresponding trimmed intersection vertex `V_trim` so `ArcLength` and `SyncPoints` pairings generate clean cone/fan rulings from `V_trim` to the opposing plane (`pairing.rs` and `ruled.rs`).\n- Snap sync points that fall inside an excised corner span directly to `V_trim` instead of shifting across adjacent flanks.\n- Update `ruled_widen::away` to derive the outward miter/offset direction from the surviving offset ring segments at trimmed vertices so per-ruling widening does not reverse or tangle.\n- Verify all ruled-surface laws (`folds`, `crossing`, `lean_law`, and 33-height `clearance` against the unhealed `product` surface) on the sewn rulings.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- Asymmetric XY/UV shapes (for example a sharp inside corner or tight fillet on XY paired with an open fillet on UV) generate clean fan rulings without phase drift, false folds, or widening reversals.\n- `clearance` catches mid-height wall gouges from bridging across a deep slot on one plane and refuses them by name.\n\nPart of #2690\n",
